Overpay and get the difference refunded!
Nanjing real estate market sees "difference compensation" again - CNTV
The Yangtze Evening Post/ZiNiu News (Reporter Ma Zuobow). On October 10th, during an interview, it was found that a long-missing "valuation agreement" has returned to the Nanjing real estate market. A property located in the New District of Jiangbei announced "price difference compensation," stating that other available units offer greater discounts than previous discounts prior to delivery, and that the developer is willing to swap houses and refund the price difference for buyers.
"Shipment Valuation Agreement" terms are not few
The property located in the New District of Jiangbei is called Chongqing Poly City Skyward Collection. Mr. Sun, who was viewing the property, told the reporter that he noticed a "statement" last weekend when he was browsing the property.
The pictures he sent to the journalists showed that the developer promised to the purchasers during the period of January 31 – February 28, 2023, if they purchased units within their signed sales contract, the developer could exchange units with better deals for those who bought prior units, and refund the difference, provided that such better deals were for other unsold units of the same floor plan, in the same building, in the same unit, or of the same type of property, offered at a higher discount than their original purchase.
Sun said that real estate agents described it as a "price-lock agreement," aimed at making buyers feel secure in their purchase and not worrying about the developer lowering prices for promotional sales. "Now they're afraid that once they buy, it will be discounted. Go to the sales office to make a fuss there is no time, and not making a fuss also feels uncomfortable."
Still, others believe that while a “price-lock agreement” does provide buyers with a sense of security, the conditions attached are not low.
Ms. Zheng, who intends to buy a first-time home in North Ring District, says that while the insured listings must be of the same type and in the same building and unit, there are very few such options available, so the "barrier" remains quite high.
There are also buyers who argue that it is not easy for them to “fight for their rights” when purchasing properties due to asymmetry of information, as sellers may not exclude offering additional discounts during sales.
Whether buyers can be retained remains to be seen.
The reporter learned from Nanjing Online Real Estate that the project obtained a sales permit for two buildings totaling 252 units last November, with户型sizes ranging from 105 sqm, 114 sqm, and 129 sqm, and a full decoration sales permit average price of 39,843 yuan per square meter.
However, just two months later, online real estate shows that the total unsold units of this project currently stand at 157, accounting for 62.3%, with 128 units in Tower 8 having 113 unsold and 124 units in Tower 7 with 44 unsold. The total number of sold units is only 33, accounting for just 13%.
Market participants explain that "price protection agreements" also appeared in Nanjing in 2008.
In August of the previous year, the housing project Xiangtang Xiyuan on Huangshan Road West in He Xi had launched the "Price Guarantee Plan" to attract homebuyers. The details were as follows: "The company solemnly promises that if there is an increase in the discount within one year, any resulting difference will be refunded to the original owners."
Subsequently in April 2011, nine housing projects in Nanjing also offered some units for sale with a “price differential compensation” commitment.
The real estate market is warming up; now it needs a ‘shot of adrenaline.’
Mr. Shen, an experienced player in the Nanjing real estate industry, stated that “price lock” agreements are also one of the marketing approaches for real estate developers.
He believes that enterprises now need more confidence than homebuyers do, and that offering a “price-lock agreement” is essentially giving them a boost.
Regarding whether he can retain homebuyers, he notes that it depends on multiple factors such as regulatory policies and loan thresholds, and it remains to be seen at this time.
China's rescue team continues to conduct rescue operations in Turkey and has rescued four trapped personnel - Xinhua News Agency.
Xinhua News Agency February 11 – According to a notice on the website of the Ministry of Emergency Management on February 11, China's rescue team, which was searching in Turkey, dispatched three operational teams and 45 rescuers on February 10, rescuing one person who was trapped.
Dispatched two search assessment teams to evaluate and investigate 15 buildings on Voddabash Street.
So far, 4 people have been rescued, 5 bodies have been found, and life signs and risks assessments have been conducted on 25 severely damaged buildings.
The rescue forces will adjust their rescue efforts scientifically according to the actual situation of the disaster area and on-site conditions, and carry out sustained rescue operations.
The rescue team obtained rescue appeal information through multiple channels such as embassies, local governments, and UN relief organizations, and verified each case through online inquiries, on-site searches, and other methods.
Brief the Chinese Hong Kong rescue team on the current rescue environment and conditions of building collapses, and conduct joint search operations.
Currently serving as the Regional Coordination System (SSC5) with the Italian rescue team, and dispatching three members to work at the 5th RescEU Coordination Center. Communicating with multiple teams from countries including Italy, the United Kingdom, Serbia, Slovakia, and Oman, I have gained an understanding of the rescue operations conducted by both the UN rescue organization and various national rescue teams.
The rescue team continuously strengthens safety management and force support, adhering to the principle of "unified command, safety first," enhancing safety control at the rescue site, reinforcing requirements for rescue work discipline, and specifying safety precautions.
Maintain continuous on-duty and sentry work systems, strengthen camp security management.
Medical personnel of the rescue team provide daily health check-ups for the members to enhance medical safeguards for key personnel. Currently, all members of the rescue team are in good health, and they are conducting disinfection and sterilization of the camp area.
After establishing the campsite, the logistics support team erected a total of 26 jumbo tents across four categories: command communication, equipment storage, medical decontamination, and living accommodation, as well as dog kennels, to ensure the provision of over 30 sets of rescue equipment at the scene.
Kim Jong-un interacts closely with his daughter while his wife is left on the side.
(Comprehensive 11th Edition) North Korea held its 75th anniversary military parade on Sunday evening, with Kim Ji-won, the leader Kim Jong-un's daughter, not only attending but also standing alongside her father on the rostrum.
North Korean state media released footage on Sunday showing Kim Jong Ae hugging her father close, making tender eye contact and whispering to him several times. She gently held her father’s cheek with her hands and even touched his chest. The father-daughter interaction was broadcast nationwide.
However, First Lady Li Xuezhu could only step aside.
According to reports from South Korea’s “Chosun Ilbo” among others, Kim Jong-un and Lee Seo-joo’s daughter Kim Jong-ae attended an official photo taken on the evening of July 7th, where she was notably seated in the middle C position between her parents. The following day, on the 75th anniversary of the founding of the People’s Army, she was seen alongside Kim Jong-un on the reviewing stand.
North Korean state media, CCTV of the Democratic People's Republic of Korea, later released footage of the parade, revealing more scenes of father-daughter affection.
Kim Jong-un looked several times at his daughter on the dais, both of their smiles never fading. They whispered to each other in their ears, and Kim Chong-un once held both cheeks of his father with both hands. Kim Jong-un responded with a radiant smile.
Other state media images show that Kim Kumyeon touched her father’s face repeatedly with her hands when she sat on an indoor sofa with Kim Jong-un, and she touched Kim Jong-un’s chest with her hand as they walked arm in arm with their father.
And First Lady Li Xuequ only walked behind or sat on the side of her husband and daughter, always maintaining a few steps distance from them.
Korean media noted that since Kim Myong-ah first made public appearances after testing the Naro-17 missile on November 18, 2021, her chances of appearing in public events have increased over the past three months, and she has now appeared in official settings five times so far.
North Korean state media used honorific terms such as "cherished descendants" and "honored descendants" when mentioning Kim Jae-woong, and aired clips where he repeatedly shouted his unwavering support for the white-blooded lineage from the stands while watching the military parade.
These signs have raised doubts about Kim Jong-chul’s pre-ordained position as the successor to the Kim regime, with The Washington Post analyzing it as “a signal from Kim Jong-un to put his teenage daughter in a position of succession.” However, others argue that such an assessment is too hasty, noting that there are still various possibilities given that Kim Jong-un has a son.
"The E Fund Account is here: CSRC authorizes development, all funds under an investor's name can be aggregated and queried - Economic Observer – Professional Financial News Website."
Difficult to collect account information due to the complex channels for purchasing funds?
Always forgetting about the "slush fund"?
The issues of the villagers will soon be resolved.
February 10, the China Securities Regulatory Commission (CSRC) announced that the "Fund E Account" APP has been launched and is currently undergoing public trial operation on various mobile app stores.
According to the introduction, the "Fund E Account" provides a one-stop service for individual investors to query information about publicly offered fund accounts and holdings, aiming to address industry pain points such as investors forgetting their accounts and facing cumbersome querying processes.
According to data from Wind, as of the end of 2022, there were 156 fund management companies in China, managing a fund size of approximately 26 trillion yuan; there were 167 fund registration institutions for open-end funds, and 411 fund sales institutions.
Each share registration institution has an independent account system and there is no industry-wide unified query channel.
Industry sources indicate that at the end of 2021, China's fund investors exceeded 720 million people, meaning half of the country’s population had invested in fund products.
Previously, investors had to check their purchase status with different sales institutions individually, but through the “Fund E Account,” all sales channels can be queried, making it clear at a glance how many funds they hold.
"What is the 'Fund E Account' APP?"
According to relevant documents, "Fund E Account" APP is an official mobile application developed and constructed by the China Securities Depository and Clearing Corporation with approval from the China Securities Regulatory Commission, offering a one-stop query of the holdings of all market open-end fund products for investors.
Investors can conveniently and quickly track their holdings of open-end fund shares from different fund managers across various channels through the 'Fund E Account', significantly enhancing query efficiency.
Specifically, investors can query through the “Fund E Account” information including: fund account information opened with all public offering fund managers, trading account information opened with public offering fund sales institutions, and the holdings of products such as open-end shares of publicly offered securities investment funds and collective asset management plans established by securities companies where the number of investors is not subject to a limit of 200 people.
Li Yuqian, head of business operations at the Shanghai Stock Exchange Fund Evaluation Research Center, told Economic Observer that investors can get all information about their off-exchange public funds through the "Fund E Account" App in one place, helping them recover "forgotten assets." More importantly, it enables comprehensive aggregation of fund investment information across accounts for clients, allowing them to better monitor and understand their investment status in real time, accurately, and comprehensively. This helps clients optimize their fund portfolio more effectively and better plan their financial arrangements.
How to register and use?
The reporter noted that currently, the "Fund E Account" APP has been launched in the app stores of Huawei, Apple, Xiaomi, OPPO, and vivo, but the APP is still in an open trial operation phase, requiring users to fill in an invite code to register. Investors can obtain the invite code by contacting the fund management company they hold.
A customer service personnel from a mid-to-large-sized public fund management company in Shanghai provided an invitation code consisting of six digits to an Economic Observer reporter and said, "During the app trial run phase, China Securities Depository and Clearing Corporation provides each fund manager with a certain number of invitation codes. Investors call to obtain them, and we provide them all."
Users will no longer need an invite code to register when open registration is activated after the trial run ends.
Please provide the Chinese text you would like translated.
The reporter registered and completed a query of their account by downloading and using the related documents posted on the CSRC website, which is titled "Fund E Account." The entire process took only a few minutes and mainly consisted of four steps: user registration, real-name authentication, binding of fund accounts, and querying public offering funds.
After completing the real-name authentication, click on the "Assets" fund binding button. All fund products purchased through various fund sales platforms by the journalist will be displayed in the binding options list (accounts that can be bound). After binding, one can see the total asset value of the invested funds and start using the querying function.
Notably, the "Fund E Account" provides query services for investors but does not facilitate subscription, redemption, or trading.
The data displayed in the "Fund E Account" generally corresponds to the date three trading days prior to the date of the query (T day).
For instance, on February 10th, opening the “Fund E Account” displays the total assets, shares, and net asset value shown on the Assets page corresponding to the three trading days prior to that date, which is February 7th.
