Strongly recommend Amazon to stop using EMS!
Five stars for the product, one star for logistics, average three stars.
Don't know why Amazon would send it via EMS; that's widely considered unreliable, right? After all, computers are valuable items!
After placing the order, the delivery was expected to arrive on the 20th, so everyone waited for three days at home.
Why does it take four to five days to send something from Xiamen to Fuzhou?
This morning on the 22nd, I finally checked the logistics and it arrived in Fuzhou. I was preparing to happily receive it when, without any phone calls or messages, I checked the logistics later that evening and found that it had been signed for midday, with the note indicating it was signed by the recipient themselves!
I was instantly shocked!
Who am I? Where am I? Is this computer really mine?
Damn near questioning my life, right?
I finally had to go to the collection point to fetch the computer back.
The specific reason, in simple terms, was that the delivery guy mixed up two tracking numbers; fortunately, the package didn't get lost.
I strongly suggest that Amazon don't use EMS anymore, and I definitely won't buy from them again if they start using EMS for their deliveries.
Awaiting supplier's response
The packaging has no labels; simply call the supplier and say that there is no label because it is genuine. If in doubt, send a sample to Johnson & Johnson for verification using old parts, and leave your license plate number and phone number. They promised to send a text message to notify me to input my information into the warranty card on their website. I haven't received any such message yet though.
The packaging is damaged; time will reveal the quality of the product.
The outer packaging is severely damaged, but the inner box seems new. The instructions, however, appear to be not new and were probably installed in September, during storage. I hope they won't be defective by the time I receive them. Could you please explain why several customers mentioned the damage to the packaging while Amazon can seem unaffected? Thank you!
The things are good, but platform bureaucracy remains.
The hard drive is of very good quality with an excellent value-to-price ratio, and it's even cheaper than in Hong Kong. It's definitely recommended to purchase if you're not in a hurry and can tolerate the logistics.
But it must be said that Amazon's bureaucracy remains the same, unchanged from when I swore I would never use it again, and you can never track the actual shipping status, information always arrives several weeks later, and you can never complain – that is so bureaucratic!
It has been days since the shipment arrived, but the logistics information still shows that you will receive the goods 10 days from now!
Incorrect image
I thought I would receive headphones like Figure 1, but instead received headphones like Figure 2. Even the mismatch between the picture and the item is fine, but what does it mean that the left and right volumes are unequal?
While the names are the same, please be cautious and also kindly ask Amazon's representative to replace the correct image promptly. Thank you very much.
The worst online shopping experience
After placing the order on September 28th, the system showed it had been shipped, but I did not receive the goods until October 12th.
Checking the status of an Amazon order, the seller has not provided a tracking number, so I can't find where the order is.
So I sent an email to the seller asking if they could provide a tracking number, but received no response for two days.
As a last resort, I contacted Amazon customer service, who provided the seller's phone number. I called the store and after several attempts, the call connected. The seller informed me that the package had been lost and that a new one could be sent immediately.
Although I was very angry, since the computer was urgently needed, I didn't say much to the seller and just asked for it to be sent to me immediately.
So, the next day, I called to ask if it had shipped yet?
The seller says it's not available yet; it will be shipped in the afternoon.
I called again in the afternoon, and the seller said they would definitely ship it, with shipping after 5 or 6 PM. By the time I called at 7 PM, there was no answer on the phone.
On the third morning, I called again to ask if the shipment had been sent out?
May I have the order number?
The seller said they haven't shipped it yet. They told me to order from another place if I need it urgently, and that if not, it will be shipped in the afternoon.
There's nothing I can do; placing an order from another place will take much longer.
All I can do is beg the seller to ship out quickly.
Finally, after countless phone trackings, I received the computer on October 16.
As for the quality of the computer, I don't know since it was bought for someone else. I'll add a review later.
