After I received the delivery, the delivery person called me and said that I didn't want it and tried to cancel the order but failed. The delivery person then took it back and asked me to sign for it first before I could apply for a refund.
When applying for a refund, they inform that food items cannot be returned once received; this is the same statement that they provide upon delivery – returns are not accepted once the item has been received.
I have bought items that cannot be returned under policy from both JD and Suning before, including milk and diapers, and contacted customer service in both cases where they were able to get a refund. Even for diapers from JD that had an overwhelming odor after opening, I was able to get a refund through customer service. However, at Amazon, this doesn't work for me.
The rules are dead, and people are alive. How did you handle contacting your customer service?
Tell me to either take it myself or let the delivery person buy it themselves. After all, delivery people don't have an easy job; why should I make them pay for something they didn't purchase?
Okay, I won’t back out either. I’ll take it, but I must give your service a score of 1 out of 5.
Amazon's own-brand should not carry such products.
Buy during product sales events when the price is not low; it's also a good product based on reviews.
Upon receiving the actual product, I was stunned. The surface of the item had extensive wear and tear, and there were other areas of wear and tear as well. It was either a second-hand item or old, and I will post some pictures later.
I am returning the item, and the people from the manufacturer said it was due to transportation damage. Isn't that ridiculous?
How could there be wear and tear within the product?
There are only two possibilities: either defective or used items, or I intentionally damaged the product and returned it.
Objectively, I have no evidence to prove that I damaged the product, but considering my shopping record on Amazon, I believe such a product should not be in Amazon's own-brand items. Customers choose Amazon's own-brand because they trust it; customer wins, we win, the victory of the customer is also the victory of the manufacturer. Let's all work together to improve this. Thank you.
A satisfactory watch
It is definitely genuine; I had it checked at the boutique, and the watch looks very nice with fine craftsmanship and ample materials. With an imported mechanical movement, it has substance, something that cannot be compared to those $300-$400 mechanical watches. This is indeed of real value.
The watch keeps accurate time with errors within acceptable limits. There is a gemstone appraisal certificate inside the watch box. The twelve o'clock position on the dial features real diamonds; it is suitable to wear and makes for a good gift.
The Bentley Tablet is quite good.
Compact and spacious
Its lightness and large opening are nice to me, but two separate compartment bags feel a bit redundant; I'm not sure what to put in them.
After buying, I found another brand that was very similar on Overseas Purchase from Meituan for less than two hundred yuan.
The first time I bought it, everything was faulty; all the lights were flashing and it didn't work properly.
Requesting a return, but the shipment to Shanghai is already three days old and hasn't been sent over.
The call to delivery isn't answered.
The courier company says they only have that contact information.
Amazon has no place to report complaints.
No request was made for delayed delivery, but I received a message saying my request for delayed delivery was being delayed without any reason.
What else is there to say about transshipment issues?
A poor shopping experience makes me doubt the effectiveness of Amazon's logistics and control systems.
Estimate that I won't be able to get it today either.
